1
00:03:28,125 --> 00:03:34,125
He's dying to become a chef.

2
00:06:56,250 --> 00:07:02,250
Ratatouille is a animation, comedy, family film directed by Brad Bird.

3
00:10:24,375 --> 00:10:30,375
Remy, a resident of Paris, has quite a sophisticated palate.

4
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:58,500
He would love to become a chef so he can create and enjoy
culinary masterpieces to his heart's delight.

5
00:17:20,625 --> 00:17:26,625
The only problem is, Remy is a rat.

6
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:54,750
When he winds up in the sewer beneath one of Paris' finest restaurants,
Remy finds himself ideally placed to realize his dream.

7
00:24:16,875 --> 00:24:22,875
He forms an unusual alliance with the restaurants rookie employee, and together they work through challenges stemming from Head Chef
Skinner, Remy’s colony, and renowned food critic Anton Ego, who strikes fear in the hearts of chefs all throughout France.

8
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Remy (voice), played by Patton Oswalt.

9
00:31:13,125 --> 00:31:19,125
Skinner (voice), played by Ian Holm.

10
00:34:41,250 --> 00:34:47,250
Linguini (voice), played by Lou Romano.

11
00:38:09,375 --> 00:38:15,375
Django (voice), played by Brian Dennehy.

12
00:41:37,500 --> 00:41:43,500
Emile (voice), played by Peter Sohn.

13
00:45:05,625 --> 00:45:11,625
Anton Ego (voice), played by Peter O'Toole.

14
00:48:33,750 --> 00:48:39,750
Ratatouille ( RAT-ə-TOO-ee) is a 2007 American animated comedy-drama film written and
directed by Brad Bird, from a story by Jan Pinkava, Jim Capobianco and Bird.

15
00:52:01,875 --> 00:52:07,875
Produced by Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures, the film stars the voices of Patton Oswalt, Lou
Romano, Ian Holm, Janeane Garofalo, Peter O'Toole, Brian Dennehy, Peter Sohn and Brad Garrett.

16
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:36,000
The title refers to the French dish ratatouille, and also
references the species of the main character, a rat.

17
00:58:58,125 --> 00:59:04,125
Set mostly in Paris, the plot follows a young rat Remy (Oswalt) who dreams of becoming a chef at Auguste Gusteau's (Garrett) restaurant
and tries to achieve his goal by forming an unlikely alliance with the restaurant's garbage boy Alfredo Linguini (Romano).

18
01:02:26,250 --> 01:02:32,250
Development for Ratatouille began in 2000 when Pinkava wrote the original concepts of
the film, although he was never formally named the director of the film.

19
01:05:54,375 --> 01:06:00,375
In 2005, following Pinkava's departure from Pixar for lacking confidence in the story
development, Bird was approached to direct the film and revise the story.

20
01:09:22,500 --> 01:09:28,500
Bird and some of the film's crew members also visited Paris for inspiration.

21
01:12:50,625 --> 01:12:56,625
To create the food animation used in the film, the crew
consulted chefs from both France and the United States.

22
01:16:18,750 --> 01:16:24,750
Lewis interned at Thomas Keller's The French Laundry restaurant, where
Keller developed the confit byaldi, a dish used in the film.

23
01:19:46,875 --> 01:19:52,875
Michael Giacchino composed the Paris-inspired music for the film.

24
01:23:15,000 --> 01:23:21,000
Ratatouille premiered on June 22, 2007, at the Kodak Theatre in Los Angeles,
California, with its general release on June 29, in the United States.

25
01:26:43,125 --> 01:26:49,125
The film became a critical and commercial success,
grossing $623.7 million worldwide.

26
01:30:11,250 --> 01:30:17,250
It finished its theatrical run as the sixth highest-grossing film of 2007 and the
year's second highest-grossing animated film (behind Shrek the Third).

27
01:33:39,375 --> 01:33:45,375
The film received widespread acclaim for its screenplay,
animation, humor, voice acting, and Giacchino's score.

28
01:37:07,500 --> 01:37:13,500
It also won the Academy Award for Best Animated Feature and was
nominated for several more, including Best Original Screenplay.

29
01:40:35,625 --> 01:40:41,625
Ratatouille was later voted one of the hundred greatest motion pictures of the 21st
century by a 2016 poll of international critics conducted by the BBC.

30
01:44:03,750 --> 01:44:09,750
The film explores themes of work, sibling relationship,
paris, france, expensive restaurant, river.

31
01:47:31,875 --> 01:47:37,875
The tone is lighthearted.
